.TH "EPX" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx \- command\-line client for the Emporix Commerce APIs
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx [flags]
epx [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Command\-line client for the Emporix Commerce APIs.
.PP
Credentials are read from the environment:
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
EMPORIX_TENANT, EMPORIX_CLIENT_ID, EMPORIX_CLIENT_SECRET (and optionally EMPORIX_API_URL).
.fi
.RE
.PP
Where none of these is set, a profile (\fBepx profile add\fR) gives them, its client secret from the OS keychain: the profile that \fB\-\-profile\fR names, else EPX_PROFILE, else the default profile (\fBepx profile use\fR). The two never mix, and naming a profile while one is set is a usage error. \fB\-\-tenant\fR overrides the tenant of either. A profile\(aqs default site and language apply where a command needs a site or shows translations and the flag is not given, on the profile\(aqs tenant.
.PP
Exit codes: 0 success, 1 error, 2 invalid usage or configuration, 3 authentication or missing scopes, 4 not found, 5 conflict: a write that Emporix answered with 409 Conflict, as when the item changed since it was read or exists already, or a \fBunits update\fR or \fBcatalogs patch\fR with metadata.version answered with 404 Not Found, as the Unit and Catalog services answer a stale version. A 403 Forbidden that the help of a command calls a refusal of its input exits 1.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
Every command takes these options.
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Help for epx.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile <name>\fR
Profile to use (default from EPX_PROFILE, else the default profile).
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant <string>\fR
Emporix tenant (default from EMPORIX_TENANT, else the profile).
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout <duration>\fR
Timeout for each HTTP request. Default: \fB30s\fR.
